  <prompt>
    Configure the Responsive-Intelligence rules as **Binding rows + `sprk_matchconditions`** (e.g. "urgency=High AND category=Court/Deadline → create Event + notify assignee"), confirm the privilege signal is **AI-FLAG-only, never a decision** (ADR-015), and add the **gate-enforcement + end-to-end fan-out tests** that close FR-19. Rules are declarative config (Binding + `sprk_matchconditions`), NOT new hard-coded branches — reuse the EventRules Binding/Action model wired in task 052.

    Implement per the gate-050 boundary: consume `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams; do NOT fork `Services/Ai/` internals. This is the wave's verification task — the tests are the primary deliverable alongside the rule config.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF/AI engineer + test author. Authoritative on the EventRules Binding/Action + `sprk_matchconditions` config model, ADR-015 privilege-flag-only, and ADR-038 KEEP-path test categories. Works within the r2-core boundary + BFF hygiene governance.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Responsive-Intelligence rules are expressed as Binding rows + `sprk_matchconditions` (declarative, no new hard-coded branches). Privilege is verified AI-FLAG-only (never auto-decided) end to end. A test suite proves: (a) `sprk_matchconditions` match → the configured artifacts (Event/Task/Notification) are created; (b) all EventRules gates (cost cap, opt-out, explicit-command supersede, M4 confidence) are enforced; (c) privilege is flagged, never decided; (d) full fan-out from `communication_assessed` fire → OutputRouter → executors works end to end. All tests follow ADR-038 KEEP paths; build clean; publish-size + CVE reported; `/conflict-check` clean.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-19 acceptance: "an assessed communication creates the rule-configured artifacts; gates enforced; privilege only flagged, never decided (ADR-015)." Task 052 wired the fan-out plumbing + gate reuse; task 053 added the Triage narrative. This task lands the *configuration* that binds category/urgency conditions to artifact creation, and the *tests* that prove the whole loop — the FR-19 closing evidence.
