  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `notes/w5-ai-coordination.md` + `EventRulesService.cs` Binding/Action model + `sprk_matchconditions` shape. Run `/conflict-check` scoped to `Services/Ai/`.</step>
    <step order="2">Author the rule config as Binding rows + `sprk_matchconditions` for the worked example ("urgency=High AND category=Court/Deadline → create Event + notify assignee") plus the minimal set needed to exercise each gate. Declarative only — no new hard-coded rule branches.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm the privilege signal path is flag-only: trace it through EventRules → OutputRouter and verify no rule/gate makes a privilege *decision*.</step>
    <step order="4">Write gate-enforcement tests (one per gate): cost cap blocks over-budget fan-out; opt-out suppresses; explicit-command supersedes; M4 confidence gate withholds low-confidence fan-out.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the privilege-flag-only test: a privilege-flagged assessment sets the flag but does not auto-decide or auto-route on privilege (ADR-015).</step>
    <step order="6">Write the end-to-end fan-out test in `tests/integration/seam/**`: fire `communication_assessed` with a matching payload → assert `sprk_event` + `appnotification` created via the configured Binding (and `task` where configured).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + the seam suite; confirm green. Verify tests sit in ADR-038 KEEP paths (no banned patterns).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet publish -c Release ... -o deploy/api-publish/` (report size + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (no new HIGH CVE).</step>
    <step order="9.5">Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONAL (TEST-MODIFYING): `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-015/013/038). Address Critical findings. `/conflict-check` clean before PR.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 054 ✅ (W5 complete). Update `current-task.md` (record rule-config location + test inventory; advance / or W5 done).</step>
  </steps>

